+## Pipeline
+
+### 1. Extraction
+
+`process_extraction()` in `extraction.py`:
+
+1. Formats recent conversation turns as `[User]: ...` / `[Assistant]: ...`
+2. Prepends conversation summary when available
+3. Calls the extraction model (`gpt-4o-mini` path in current benchmarked flows)
+4. Calibrates confidence with linguistic hedge/strength heuristics
+5. Validates extracted facts against user-centric filters
+6. Retries poor extractions with a broader coverage hint
+7. Logs the full extraction result to `memory_extraction_log`
+
+Assistant-message extraction remains selective: the system only keeps assistant content when it clearly encodes something about the user (`you` / `your` style references), not general assistant exposition.
+
+### 2. Deduplication / Supersession
+
+`deduplicate_facts()` in `dedup.py` compares extracted facts to active memories using embedding similarity plus slot-aware logic.
+
+Configured thresholds come from `orchestrator/config.py`:
+
+| Scenario | Threshold |
+|---|---:|
+| Merge | `0.90` |
+| Supersede (generic) | `0.82` |
+| Supersede (same slot) | `0.65` |
+
+Notes:
+
+- Slot families and `.current` slots trigger family-aware cleanup / closure behavior.
+- Contradiction metadata is advisory and written into `metadata`; it does not block supersession.
+- The contradiction model is driven by `background_reasoning_model` from config, not a fixed hardcoded `kimi-k2.5` model name.
 
